["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>The forecast is for the valley. You are on the ridge. Clouds, pressure and wind give you hours of warning about snow, rain, thunder and wind shifts, so you change the plan before the weather changes it for you.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Three cloud levels: high wispy ice clouds called cirrus, middle grey sheets called alto clouds, and low puffy cumulus or flat stratus near the ground.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#e7f0f7\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"14\" y=\"26\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Three cloud levels</text><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#868e96\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#868e96\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\"/><path d=\"M40 70 C 60 58, 85 60, 110 48\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#9aa5b1\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M50 78 C 70 68, 95 70, 120 58\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#9aa5b1\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M250 60 C 270 48, 295 50, 320 38\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#9aa5b1\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M260 68 C 280 58, 305 60, 330 48\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#9aa5b1\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"390\" y=\"60\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">High: cirrus</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"90\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#868e96\" text-anchor=\"start\">ice, wispy</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"130\" width=\"200\" height=\"22\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#c9d3dc\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"390\" y=\"150\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Mid: alto</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"175\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#868e96\" text-anchor=\"start\">grey sheets</text><g transform=\"translate(80 240) scale(1.2)\"><path d=\"M-30 10 C -40 10, -40 -6, -26 -6 C -24 -20, -6 -22, 0 -12 C 6 -24, 28 -20, 26 -4 C 40 -4, 40 10, 28 10 Z\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#9aa5b1\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(170 235) scale(1.0)\"><path d=\"M-30 10 C -40 10, -40 -6, -26 -6 C -24 -20, -6 -22, 0 -12 C 6 -24, 28 -20, 26 -4 C 40 -4, 40 10, 28 10 Z\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#9aa5b1\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/></g><text x=\"390\" y=\"240\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Low: cumulus,</text><text x=\"270\" y=\"258\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">stratus</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"280\" width=\"400\" height=\"20\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>High wisps, mid grey sheets, low puffs: three levels <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Watch which way they change: lowering and thickening means wet weather coming <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this lesson adds</summary><ul><li>How weather moves deer (snow, fronts, moon) is in <a href=\"#/s/weather-moon/0\">Weather, moon and what moves game</a>. This lesson is about reading the sky and air for your own plan and safety.</li><li>Ten basic cloud types by level (95%, NOAA JetStream, World Meteorological Organization classes):<ul><li>High: cirrus, cirrocumulus, cirrostratus.</li><li>Mid: altocumulus, altostratus, nimbostratus.</li><li>Low: stratocumulus, stratus, cumulus, cumulonimbus.</li></ul></li><li>Wind is the next lesson: <a href=\"#/s/wind-mastery/0\">Wind mastery</a>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Sign</th><th>Usually means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cirrus, then a halo, then grey</td><td>Warm front, rain or snow within about a day <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Puffy clouds growing tall</td><td>Showers or thunder later <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Anvil top</td><td>Thunderstorm <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Pressure falling</td><td>Low or front coming <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Wind swings to W or NW, colder</td><td>Cold front passed <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Clear, calm night</td><td>Frost, valley fog, cold dawn <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Higher up</td><td>Colder: rain below, snow above <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the key points in full</summary><ol><li>Ten cloud types in three levels (95%, NOAA).</li><li>Warm front sequence: cirrus, cirrostratus (halo), altostratus, nimbostratus (70%, Met Office and textbook sources agree on order, not timing).</li><li>Cumulonimbus is \"the thunderstorm cloud\", tall with an anvil shaped top (95%, NOAA). It can bring hail <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Behind a cold front winds shift from south to west or northwest, the dewpoint drops and pressure rises (70%, NWS text via secondary source).</li><li>With your back to the wind, low pressure is on your left in the northern hemisphere (75%, Buys Ballot's law, Wikipedia).</li><li>Cold air drains down slopes at night and pools in valleys (75%, USDA Forest Service Fire Weather handbook via Forest Encyclopedia).</li><li>Thunder heard? Go to a hard topped vehicle and wait 30 minutes after the last thunder (85%, US National Weather Service).</li></ol></details>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"4\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>Four skies before the rain</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 4</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"High wispy cirrus streaks across a blue sky, often the first sign of an approaching warm front.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"26\" cy=\"26\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Cirrus: mares tails</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"50\" width=\"400\" height=\"200\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#e7f0f7\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M60 120 C 80 108, 105 110, 130 98\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#9aa5b1\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M70 128 C 90 118, 115 120, 140 108\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#9aa5b1\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M200 90 C 220 78, 245 80, 270 68\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#9aa5b1\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M210 98 C 230 88, 255 90, 280 78\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#9aa5b1\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M260 150 C 280 138, 305 140, 330 128\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#9aa5b1\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M270 158 C 290 148, 315 150, 340 138\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#9aa5b1\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"250\" width=\"400\" height=\"10\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"282\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Often the first sign of a warm front</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> Cirrus streaks: often the first sign.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A thin milky veil of cirrostratus covers the sky with a ring of light, a halo, around the sun.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"26\" cy=\"26\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Halo: cirrostratus</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"50\" width=\"400\" height=\"200\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#e7f0f7\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"60\" width=\"400\" height=\"180\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe8f0\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\" opacity=\".7\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"140\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#f2c70c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"140\" r=\"55\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#f2c70c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"250\" width=\"400\" height=\"10\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"282\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Thin veil, ring around sun or moon</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> A halo round the sun or moon: thin cirrostratus.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A grey sheet of altostratus; the sun shows dimly as if through frosted glass.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"26\" cy=\"26\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Altostratus: grey sheet</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"50\" width=\"400\" height=\"200\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#e7f0f7\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"60\" width=\"400\" height=\"180\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#b7c2cc\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"140\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#f6f1d0\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\" opacity=\".6\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"250\" width=\"400\" height=\"10\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"282\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sun looks like through frosted glass</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> Grey sheet, sun like frosted glass: altostratus.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Dark grey nimbostratus covers the sky with steady rain or snow.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"26\" cy=\"26\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Nimbostratus: rain or snow</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"50\" width=\"400\" height=\"200\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#e7f0f7\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"60\" width=\"400\" height=\"120\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#7d8894\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"22\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"58\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"86\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"78\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"114\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"106\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"142\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"134\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"170\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"162\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"198\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"226\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"218\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"254\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"246\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"282\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"274\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"310\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"302\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"338\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"366\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"358\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"394\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"386\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"250\" width=\"400\" height=\"10\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"282\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Steady, long lasting</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>4.</b> Dark low grey, steady rain or snow: nimbostratus.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><ul><li>The sky lowers and thickens over hours <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: warm fronts in full</summary><ul><li>Order: cirrus, cirrostratus, altostratus, nimbostratus <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>The Met Office says cirrostratus can produce rings, spots or arcs of light around the sun or moon, and that one type means an incoming warm front will bring persistent rain within a day (75%, Met Office cirrostratus page, search preview).</li><li>Timing varies: sources give 12 to 24 hours from halo to rain, some less <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>. Treat it as \"within about a day\".</li><li>Ahead of a warm front pressure falls steadily and the rain is widespread and steady (70%, secondary source).</li><li>Hunter use (Tip): halo at evening glassing means plan B for tomorrow, rain gear in the pack, meat care plan for wet weather.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Side view of a warm front: warm air rides up over cold air. Far ahead are high cirrus, then a halo veil, then grey altostratus, then rain at the front. The sequence moves toward you.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#e7f0f7\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"14\" y=\"26\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Warm front: clouds lower and thicken</text><path d=\"M0 250 C 120 230, 260 150, 400 60 L400 250 Z\" fill=\"#f4d9c4\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\" opacity=\".6\"\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"220\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"start\">warm air rides up</text><path d=\"M30 80 C 50 68, 75 70, 100 58\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#9aa5b1\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M40 88 C 60 78, 85 80, 110 68\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#9aa5b1\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><rect x=\"130\" y=\"110\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe8f0\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><rect x=\"220\" y=\"150\" width=\"90\" height=\"22\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#b7c2cc\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><rect x=\"300\" y=\"180\" width=\"100\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#7d8894\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><line x1=\"310\" y1=\"222\" x2=\"304\" y2=\"248\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"326\" y1=\"222\" x2=\"320\" y2=\"248\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"342\" y1=\"222\" x2=\"336\" y2=\"248\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"358\" y1=\"222\" x2=\"352\" y2=\"248\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"374\" y1=\"222\" x2=\"368\" y2=\"248\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"390\" y1=\"222\" x2=\"384\" y2=\"248\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"110\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">cirrus</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"140\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">halo</text><text x=\"265\" y=\"190\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">grey</text><text x=\"350\" y=\"265\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">rain</text><line x1=\"380\" y1=\"285\" x2=\"47.7\" y2=\"285.0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"40.0,285.0 51.0,291.1 51.0,278.9\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"280\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">front moves this way</text><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"250\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"250\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Warm air rides up over cold air, so clouds come first, rain last <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Side view of a cold front: cold air pushes under warm air and throws up tall towering clouds with an anvil and heavy showers. After it passes the wind swings west or northwest, it gets colder and the pressure rises.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#e7f0f7\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"14\" y=\"26\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Cold front: fast, gusty, clears behind</text><path d=\"M60 250 C 120 250, 160 120, 190 70 L240 70 C 220 120, 230 200, 260 250 Z\" fill=\"#d0d6dc\" stroke=\"#9aa5b1\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M180 70 L280 60 L250 78 Z\" fill=\"#d0d6dc\" stroke=\"#9aa5b1\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"285\" y=\"66\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#868e96\" text-anchor=\"start\">anvil</text><line x1=\"170\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"164\" y2=\"248\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"182\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"176\" y2=\"248\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"194\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"188\" y2=\"248\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"206\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"248\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"218\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"212\" y2=\"248\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"230\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"224\" y2=\"248\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"242\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"236\" y2=\"248\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"120\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"162.3\" y2=\"200.0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"170.0,200.0 159.0,193.9 159.0,206.1\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"190\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">cold air</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"190\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"start\">warm, south wind</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"275\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Wind swings W or NW, temp drops, pressure rises.</text><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"250\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"250\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Tall clouds, gusts, a short burst of rain or snow <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>After: wind W or NW, colder, clearing, pressure rising <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: cold fronts in full</summary><ul><li>Before: winds often from the south, warm and humid <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>At the front: towering clouds, gusty winds, heavy showers or snow squalls <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>After: wind shifts west or northwest, temperature and dewpoint drop, pressure rises, skies clear (70%, NWS text via secondary source).</li><li>In the mountains, terrain channels wind and can hide the classic wind shift (75%, Fire Weather handbook: \"the effect of the mountains on the windflow usually overshadows this\").</li><li>Hunter use (Tip): the clear, cold morning after a cold front is a classic glassing morning. Snow after it brings fresh tracks; see <a href=\"#/s/snow-tracking/0\">Snow tracking</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: a small puffy cumulus cloud grows taller and taller through the afternoon until its top spreads into an anvil: a cumulonimbus thunderstorm cloud.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#e7f0f7\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"14\" y=\"26\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Puffy cloud growing tall: storm coming</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"270\" width=\"400\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(200 250)\"><path d=\"M-70 0 C -80 -20, -50 -35, -30 -30 C -20 -55, 20 -55, 30 -30 C 55 -35, 80 -20, 70 0 Z\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#9aa5b1\" stroke-width=\"2\"><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"scale\" values=\"1 1;1.1 1.8;1.15 2.9\" keyTimes=\"0;.5;1\" dur=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></path></g><path d=\"M120 95 L300 85 L262 108 L150 108 Z\" fill=\"#d0d6dc\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"6s\" dur=\"1s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></path><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"6.5s\" dur=\".5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"100\" y=\"40\" width=\"200\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#c92a2a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"64\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#c92a2a\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Anvil: thunderstorm</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>A cumulus that keeps growing by noon can be a thunderstorm by afternoon. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Flat bottomed puffs that stay small: fair weather <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Puffs that tower and spread an anvil: thunder, hail, gusts <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: thunder in full</summary><ul><li>Cumulonimbus: heavy, dense, shaped like a mountain or huge tower, with an anvil or plume top and a dark base; can bring hail (95%, NOAA).</li><li>\"When thunder roars, go indoors.\" Shelter in a substantial building or a hard topped vehicle and stay until 30 minutes after the last thunder (85%, US National Weather Service).</li><li>Lightning can strike well away from the rain (70%, US Army safety document).</li><li>Thunderstorms are less common in late October than in summer (Tip). Still: get off ridges and away from lone trees when you hear thunder.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Pressure trend table. Falling fast: a storm or front is coming. Falling slowly: clouds thickening. Steady: no big change. Rising: clearing and often colder.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pressure trend: what it usually means</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"55\" width=\"360\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#c92a2a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"48\" y=\"84\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#c92a2a\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">↓↓</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"82\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Falling fast</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"82\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Storm or front coming</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"107\" width=\"360\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"48\" y=\"136\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">↓</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"134\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Falling slowly</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"134\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Clouds thickening</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"159\" width=\"360\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"48\" y=\"188\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">→</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"186\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Steady</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"186\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">No big change</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"211\" width=\"360\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"48\" y=\"240\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">↑</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"238\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Rising</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"238\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Clearing, often colder</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"290\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#868e96\" text-anchor=\"start\">General rule (75%). The Hunt Map Weather shows the trend.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Falling: weather coming. Rising: clearing, often colder <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>The Hunt Map Weather sheet shows the 3 hour trend <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: pressure in full</summary><ul><li>Hunt Map, Weather and wind: \"Pressure ... hPa (hectopascals), rising, falling or steady over the last 3 hours\", from a weather model (99%, app; a change of more than 1 hPa counts as rising or falling).</li><li>Phone or watch barometer: sitting still, if your altitude reading climbs, the pressure is falling (85%, physics: about 8 m of altitude per hPa near sea level).</li><li>Pressure trends are general rules. Mountains and local winds can fool them (Tip).</li><li>Do deer care about pressure? The evidence is weak and mixed (65 to 80%). See <a href=\"#/s/weather-moon/0\">Weather, moon and what moves game</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Buys Ballot's law: stand with your back to the wind in the northern hemisphere and low pressure is on your left, high pressure on your right.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"14\" y=\"26\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Back to the wind: low on your left</text><g transform=\"translate(200 200) scale(1.3)\"><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"-30\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M0 -23 V2 M0 2 L-7 18 M0 2 L7 18 M0 -16 L-9 -4 M0 -16 L9 -4\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"/></g><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"280\" x2=\"200.0\" y2=\"232.7\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"200.0,225.0 193.9,236.0 206.1,236.0\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"285\" x2=\"150.0\" y2=\"247.7\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"150.0,240.0 143.9,251.0 156.1,251.0\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><line x1=\"250\" y1=\"285\" x2=\"250.0\" y2=\"247.7\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"250.0,240.0 243.9,251.0 256.1,251.0\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"260\" y=\"275\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">wind at your back</text><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"140\" r=\"34\" fill=\"#f4d9c4\" stroke=\"#c92a2a\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"150\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"30\" fill=\"#c92a2a\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">L</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"200\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#c92a2a\" text-anchor=\"start\">Low pressure,</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"216\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#c92a2a\" text-anchor=\"start\">bad weather side</text><circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"140\" r=\"34\" fill=\"#e8f2e0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"150\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"30\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">H</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"200\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" text-anchor=\"start\">High</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Back to the wind: low pressure on your left <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>The low is where the bad weather lives.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: Buys Ballot's law in full</summary><ul><li>In the northern hemisphere, with your back to the wind, low pressure is to the left and high pressure to the right (75%, Wikipedia, Buys Ballot's law, 1857).</li><li>Near the ground and in mountains it is approximate <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. Use the upper clouds' direction for a better read (Tip).</li><li>Use (Tip): if the low is to your west, weather is usually on its way, since systems here mostly move from the Pacific eastward. <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> with the forecast.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"At night cold air drains down the slopes and pools in the valley, making fog, frost and cold. On the slope above the fog it is often milder and clear. Tip: glass from above the fog.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#e7f0f7\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"14\" y=\"26\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Cold air pools in valleys at night</text><path d=\"M0 120 L90 80 L170 200 L230 200 L300 70 L400 110 L400 300 L0 300 Z\" fill=\"#c9d3b8\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M120 140 L170 200 L230 200 L285 120 Z\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\" opacity=\".85\"\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"175\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Fog, frost, cold</text><g transform=\"translate(330 82) scale(0.6)\"><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"-30\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M0 -23 V2 M0 2 L-7 18 M0 2 L7 18 M0 -16 L-9 -4 M0 -16 L9 -4\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"/></g><text x=\"190\" y=\"48\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Glass from above</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"64\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">the fog (Tip)</text><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"95\" x2=\"104.8\" y2=\"144.3\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\"/><polygon points=\"110.0,150.0 107.1,137.8 98.1,145.9\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><line x1=\"350\" y1=\"110\" x2=\"296.4\" y2=\"145.7\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\"/><polygon points=\"290.0,150.0 302.5,148.9 295.8,138.9\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"250\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Cold air drains down</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"268\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">slopes after sunset</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Clear calm nights: cold air drains down into valleys <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Morning fog or frost below, milder and clear above (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: inversions in full</summary><ul><li>Downslope flow starts first along the valley floor in the evening, deepens through the night and becomes the down valley wind; as cold air pools, pressure rises in the valley (75%, Fire Weather handbook via Forest Encyclopedia).</li><li>Down valley flow lasts through the night and weakens after sunrise <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Kamloops sits in a deep valley. Fall mornings often have valley fog or haze (Tip).</li><li>Hunter use (Tip): climb above the fog to glass; the sun hits upper slopes first and deer move to it on cold mornings. See <a href=\"#/s/hunt-map-pro/0\">Sun and shade in the Hunt Map</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A valley at 400 metres is 8 degrees Celsius. A ridge 1,000 metres higher is about 1.5 degrees: standard air cools about 6.5 degrees per 1,000 metres. Rain in the valley can be snow on the ridge.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Higher is colder</text><path d=\"M20 270 L140 200 L230 90 L300 60 L380 140 L380 270 Z\" fill=\"#c9d3b8\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"262\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"250\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Valley 400 m: 8°C</text><circle cx=\"260\" cy=\"75\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"50\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ridge 1,400 m: about 1.5°C</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"295\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#868e96\" text-anchor=\"start\">About 6.5°C colder per 1,000 m up (standard air).</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>About 6.5°C colder per 1,000 m up in standard air <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Rain at the truck can be snow on the ridge <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: temperature and height in full</summary><ul><li>Standard air cools about 6.5°C per 1,000 m of height (85%, International Standard Atmosphere). Real days vary, and inversions flip it at night.</li><li>Example: 8°C at a 400 m valley floor is about 1.5°C on a 1,400 m ridge (85%, maths).</li><li>Wind makes it feel colder still. See hypothermia in <a href=\"#/s/bush-safety/0\">Bush safety</a>.</li><li>Pack for the top of the hunt, not the truck (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A sky check. Halo, lowering grey cloud and falling pressure: rain or snow likely in about a day, plan B. Puffy clouds growing tall by noon: showers or thunder, get off ridges. Thunder heard: go to the truck and wait 30 minutes after the last thunder. Clear high pressure: cold frosty dawn, great glassing.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"30\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sky check: go, watch or get off</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"360\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"70\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Halo, lowering grey, pressure falling?</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"98\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Rain or snow likely in about a day (70%). Plan B.</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"112\" width=\"360\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"134\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Puffy clouds growing tall by noon?</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"162\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Showers or thunder. Off ridges early.</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"176\" width=\"360\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#c92a2a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"198\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Thunder heard?</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"226\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Truck, wait 30 min after last thunder.</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"240\" width=\"360\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"262\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">High pressure, clear, light wind</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"290\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Cold dawn, frost, great glassing (Tip).</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Look up every hour. Write it in your journal (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: sky check in full</summary><ul><li>Every line in the chart is a general rule, not a promise (70 to 85%, see the screens above).</li><li>Forecast first: the Hunt Map Weather and wind sheet gives wind, gusts, rain chance and the next 3 days at the map centre <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Check your regular forecast too.</li><li>Fire bans and wildfire smoke: <a href=\"#/s/bush-safety/0\">Bush safety</a>.</li><li>Weather that turns roads to grease: check road status before you drive in. See <a href=\"#/s/maps-land-status/0\">Maps 3</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A thin milky veil of cirrostratus covers the sky with a ring of light, a halo, around the sun.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"26\" cy=\"26\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Halo: cirrostratus</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"50\" width=\"400\" height=\"200\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#e7f0f7\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"60\" width=\"400\" height=\"180\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe8f0\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\" opacity=\".7\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"140\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#f2c70c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"140\" r=\"55\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#f2c70c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"250\" width=\"400\" height=\"10\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"282\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Thin veil, ring around sun or moon</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom): Ring around the moon, rain or snow soon. Pack the wet gear and hunt the morning.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Reading the valley forecast and dressing for the valley.</li><li>Ignoring a halo and a falling barometer the night before.</li><li>Staying on a ridge while a cloud grows an anvil.</li></ul></aside><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the mistakes in full</summary><ul><li>Dressing for the truck's temperature, not the ridge 1,000 m higher.</li><li>Ignoring the halo at evening glassing and the falling pressure: no rain gear the next day, a soaked deer and wet meat.</li><li>Staying on an open ridge while a cloud grows tall and dark overhead.</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>For one week, before work, look at the sky and write: cloud type, wind direction, pressure trend. Write tomorrow's guess. Check it next morning. Score yourself out of 7.</p></aside><div class=\"checklist\" data-list=\"fn-sky-week\"><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"fn-sky-week:0\"><span>Named the cloud level each morning</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"fn-sky-week:1\"><span>Noted wind direction and pressure trend</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"fn-sky-week:2\"><span>Made a guess for tomorrow</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"fn-sky-week:3\"><span>Checked the guess and scored it</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"fn-sky-week:4\"><span>Spotted a halo or a growing cumulus at least once</span></label></div>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Hook</th><th>Means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Ring around the moon, rain soon</td><td>Halo before a warm front</td></tr><tr><td>Mares' tails and mackerel scales make tall ships take in their sails</td><td>High clouds before wind and rain</td></tr><tr><td>Lower and thicker, wetter and quicker</td><td>Warm front sequence</td></tr><tr><td>Puff that grows, run from the blows</td><td>Building cumulus</td></tr><tr><td>Back to the wind, low on the left</td><td>Buys Ballot</td></tr><tr><td>Six and a half per thousand</td><td>Lapse rate</td></tr><tr><td>Thirty after thunder</td><td>Wait 30 min</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li><strong>Falling glass, foul weather passes in; rising glass, it passes out.</strong> Old sailor's line for the barometer (Tip).</li><li><strong>Clear and calm, cold and calm in the hollow.</strong> Night cold air pooling.</li><li>These rhymes are folklore. The screens above give the evidence and certainty.</li></ul></details>","<ul><li><a href=\"https://www.noaa.gov/jetstream/clouds/ten-basic-clouds\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NOAA JetStream: ten basic clouds</a>, read directly 2026-10-11: cloud levels, cumulonimbus, nimbostratus, altostratus <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://weather.metoffice.gov.uk/learn-about/weather/types-of-weather/clouds/high-clouds/cirrostratus\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Met Office: cirrostratus clouds</a>, search preview 2026-10-11: halo, warm front rain within a day <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Cold and warm front winds and pressure: <a href=\"https://weather.gov/lmk/basic-fronts\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NWS Louisville basic fronts</a> and secondary sources, search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buys_Ballot%27s_law\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikipedia: Buys Ballot's law</a>, search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://old.forestencyclopedia.net/p/p406/print_section\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Forest Encyclopedia: slope and valley winds, and general winds</a>, from Schroeder and Buck, Fire Weather, USDA Agriculture Handbook 360, 1970, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.weather.gov/safety/lightning-safety-overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">US National Weather Service: lightning safety</a>, search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul>","<ul><li>Lapse rate: International Standard Atmosphere value, general meteorology <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Hunt Map pressure trend wording: app code, read 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul>"]